  "body": "When investigating https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1395951, I found the following.\r\n\r\n- `console.log(textarea.innerHTML)` for `<textarea>ABC<LF>DEF</textarea>` outputs\r\n  - `ABC<BR>DEF` on Gecko (LF converted to `<BR>` element)\r\n  - `ABC<0x0A>DEF` on Edge and Blink\r\n- Typing ABC on `<textarea>`, then, `console.log(textarea.innerHTML)` outputs\r\n  - Same as `console.log(textarea.value)` on Gecko (if not multiple line) and Edge\r\n  - Blink returns original before typing text.  It is different of `console.log(textarea.value)`\r\n\r\nWhat's correct behavior for interoperability?  I think that Edge or Gecko's behavior may be better, but I don't know.",
